<title>HONG KONG: S. Megga says chairman died on Sept 28.</title>
<headline>S. Megga says chairman died on Sept 28.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telecommunications products maker S. Megga International Holdings Ltd said on Wednesday its chairman Leung Ray Man died on September 28.</p>
<p>S. Megga said there would be no material adverse changes to the company business operations on the death of Leung, who held 141.12 million or 24.7 percent of the company's shares.</p>
<p>The company said &quot;the directors are not aware of any changes in such shareholding at this stage&quot;.</p>
<p>An announcement would be made on appointment of a new chairman, it said. S. Megga shares were untraded at HK$0.244 in early trade. -- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
